\par \f1\b\fs28 1. What Hippocampus does\par
\f0\b0\fs24
\par
Hippocampus is a local-first macOS application that can capture screen and\par
workflow context when you enable capture. It processes captured content on the\par
Mac using OCR and local models and stores memory data in a local SQLCipher\par
database.\par
\par
The local memory pipeline does not upload captured content to a Hippocampus\par
service. Update checks and diagnostics you explicitly enable may contact their\par
stated services. Content you intentionally send to a connected external tool or\par
model is governed by that provider's terms and privacy practices.\par
\par
\par \f1\b\fs28 2. License\par
\f0\b0\fs24
\par
Subject to these terms and the licenses supplied with the software, you may\par
install and use Hippocampus on macOS devices you own or control for personal or\par
internal business purposes.\par
\par
You may not use Hippocampus to violate applicable law, capture content you do\par
